WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Your eyes are extremely sensitive, so when dealing with eye injuries, our first and most

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.680
important rule is never rub an injured eye.

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:15.040
Rubbing can push a foreign object deeper or cause it to scratch the surface of the eye,

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:17.000
making the injury much worse.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.559
As you assess the patient, ask them a few key questions.

00:00:20.559 --> 00:00:22.280
Did anything hit your eye?

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:24.600
Does it feel like something is still in there?

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:27.840
Can you open your eye and can you still see well?

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:32.400
If someone has a foreign object like dust or a small piece of debris in their eye and

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:37.560
blinking doesn't clear it, your next step is to rinse the eye with clean water.

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:42.439
If you see an item stuck under an eyelid, you can gently use sterile gauze to lift the

00:00:42.439 --> 00:00:44.799
lid and remove the visible debris.

00:00:44.799 --> 00:00:49.840
However, if the object is embedded or you simply cannot get it out, stop what you are

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:55.480
doing, cover both eyes to prevent movement, and wait for EMS to arrive.

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:59.400
When you are dealing with chemical injuries, time is of the essence.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:04.680
You must rinse the eye with clean water for at least 15 to 20 minutes without stopping.

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:09.599
When rinsing, position the head so the water flows from the inner corner of the eye toward

00:01:09.599 --> 00:01:11.220
the outer corner.

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:16.199
This prevents the chemicals from washing across the bridge of the nose and into the unaffected

00:01:16.199 --> 00:01:17.199
eye.

00:01:17.199 --> 00:01:21.639
If the person is wearing contact lenses and can remove them easily, they should do so

00:01:21.639 --> 00:01:24.440
while you continue the flushing process.

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:29.120
Before a physical hit to the eye, apply a cold pack to the area to help reduce pain

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:30.480
and swelling.

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:36.480
Call 911 immediately if they are experiencing severe pain, have any changes in their vision,

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:38.400
or if a chemical or object won't come out.

